<?xml version="1.0" ?><gpx xmlns="http://www.topografix.com/GPX/1/1" creator="GaiaGPS" version="1.1" xmlns:xsi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema-instance" xsi:schemaLocation="http://www.topografix.com/GPX/1/1 http://www.topografix.com/GPX/1/1/gpx.xsd"><wpt lat="42.973958616021065" lon="-73.07181939080232"><time>2026-09-18T01:52:16Z</time><name>Night 1: Goddard Shelter</name><desc>First night, July 3rd, 2021. Goddard shelter, next to the lean to in the tent. Rainy and cold night. SAR helo flew over us at night, searchlights beamed our tent at one point.</desc><sym>emoji-⛺</sym></wpt><wpt lat="43.05054161054804" lon="-73.01191379112846"><time>2026-09-18T01:56:59Z</time><name>Night 2, Story Spring Shelter</name><desc>2nd night of the trip, July 4th 2021. Cold and rainy again. Camped in our tent next to the shelter. Big family in the shelter.</desc><sym>emoji-⛺</sym></wpt><wpt lat="43.106153401391225" lon="-72.97211639978643"><time>2026-09-18T01:58:49Z</time><name>Night 3, Stratton  Pond</name><desc>3rd and last night of the trip, July 5 2021. Rain stopped. Camped by the mountain view / NW side of the pond. Great views in the evening and morning. Had some trouble putting my contacts in.</desc><sym>emoji-⛺</sym></wpt><rte><name>Route</name><desc>Vermont Long Trail / AT point to point hike from Bennington to Manchester Center. July 2021 with Dylan.</desc><extensions><line xmlns="http://www.topografix.com/GPX/gpx_style/0/2"><color>FF6200</color></line></extensions><rtept lat="42.885105" lon="-73.11565"><ele>410.8984375</ele><time>2026-09-18T01:45:06Z</time></rtept><rtept lat="42.88515" lon="-73.115215"><ele>411.09765625</ele><time>2026-09-18T01:45:06Z</time></rtept><rtept lat="42.885082" lon="-73.115124"><ele>411.296875</ele><time>2026-09-18T01:45:06Z</time></rtept><rtept lat="42.885021" lon="-73.115127"><ele>411.0</ele><time>2026-09-18T01:45:06Z</time></rtept><rtept lat="42.884941" lon="-73.115159"><ele>411.0</ele><time>2026-09-18T01:45:06Z</time></rtept><rtept lat="42.88